# Claude Code workflow reference

Env-specific facts; decisions and their triggers live in the chezmoi repo's `docs/decisions.md`.
If behavior seems changed, verify (claude-code-guide) and update its template in the chezmoi repo.

## Models

- Driver: `{{ index .subagent_tiers.claude .agents.claude.defaults.tier }}` at effort `{{ .agents.claude.defaults.reasoning_effort }}`, pinned under `modelSettings` for every pin so a `/model` escalation keeps it.
- Escalate effort first: `/effort xhigh` keeps the prompt cache. `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`
  is escalation-only: for an ambiguous root-cause or architecture problem
  where the driver at higher effort fell short, start a fresh session with
  `claude --model {{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`. Do not `/model` a grown session: each model has its own
  cache, so the next request re-reads the whole history uncached at the frontier rate, and
  `/model <name>` saves it as the default until the next apply. In a
  frontier-model session don't fork — forks inherit it.
- Roles render from `subagents` in agents.yaml; `docs/decisions.md` records each why. Pins do not
  follow `/model`; a child without explicit effort inherits session effort.

